-- WITHAL written as a TYPICALLY default is no literal, and that is the one thing
-- the author is told (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md T1, ruled by Meng
-- 2026-10-09). A default must be a fixed value written out.
--
-- This used to add a second, false error. This module's own records are put
-- where a construction finds their defaults only AFTER the defaults of record
-- fields and of rule inputs have been checked, so `Inner` was not yet known as a
-- record there and was reported as "one of the alternatives of a type declared
-- with ONE OF". A record is now told from an alternative by its declaration.

DECLARE Inner HAS
  a IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 1

-- a field's default
DECLARE Outer HAS
  inner IS AN Inner TYPICALLY (Inner WITHAL)
  n     IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2

#EVAL Outer WITHAL

-- a rule input's default
GIVEN p IS AN Inner TYPICALLY (Inner WITHAL)
GIVETH A NUMBER
f p MEANS p's a

#EVAL f WITH p IS Inner WITH a IS 5
